How would you implement an LRU cache with TTL? What happens if an entry expires but is still in the DLL?


1. Active Expiration

A background thread periodically checks for expired entries:

Background Thread
       ↓
Check expired entries
       ↓
Remove from Map
       ↓
Remove from DLL



2. Lazy Expiration

Store expiration time in the node:

class Node {
    int key;
    int val;
    long expiryTime;
}

On get():

get(key)
   ↓
Find node
   ↓
Is expired?
   ├── Yes → Remove from Map + DLL → return -1
   └── No  → Move to HEAD → return value

On put():

Existing key
   ↓
Update value
Update expiryTime
Move to HEAD

This is simple and works well if expired entries aren't a problem until accessed.



